# Deck the Halls, single-line melody (repertoire plan: deck-the-halls). The Welsh tune (Nos
# Galan) in G, first position. Lines 1, 2 and 4 start high on string 2, fret 3 (D) and step down
# the scale: D. C B A | G A B G. The fa-la-la of lines 1 and 2 ends with the leading note F#
# (string 4, fret 4, finger 4) rising to G. Line 3 climbs through the one sharp the tune adds,
# C# (string 2, fret 2), to the top G (string 1, fret 3). Line 4's fa-la-la starts on four
# repeated E's (open string 1) and walks down the scale home: E E E E D. C | B A G (mi re do).
# Fingers: first position, finger = fret (1 on fret 1, 2 on fret 2, 3 on fret 3, 4 on fret 4).
# The teacher strums G, C and D7.
title: Deck the Halls
id: deck-the-halls
composer: Traditional Welsh
source: Welsh tune (Nos Galan) printed in 1794; English words by Thomas Oliphant (1862); arranged for Sixstring Academy
arranger: Sixstring Academy
licence: Public domain; this arrangement is original to Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 2
tags: melody, christmas, dotted rhythm, lyrics, first position
tempo: 108
time: 4/4
key: G

track: Melody
role: lead
[Line 1]
| "G" q. 2:3{3} e 2:1{1} q 2:0 3:2{2} | "C" 3:0 3:2 "G" 2:0 3:0 | "D7" e 3:2 2:0 2:1 3:2 "G" q. 2:0 e 3:2 | "G" q 3:0 "D7" 4:4{4} "G" h 3:0 |
lyrics: Deck the halls with boughs of hol- ly, Fa la la la la, la la la la.
[Line 2]
| "G" q. 2:3 e 2:1 q 2:0 3:2 | "C" 3:0 3:2 "G" 2:0 3:0 | "D7" e 3:2 2:0 2:1 3:2 "G" q. 2:0 e 3:2 | "G" q 3:0 "D7" 4:4 "G" h 3:0 |
lyrics: 'Tis the sea- son to be jol- ly, Fa la la la la, la la la la.
[Line 3]
| "D7" q. 3:2 e 2:0 q 2:1 3:2 | "G" q. 2:0 e 2:1 "D7" q 2:3 3:2 | "G" e 2:0 2:2{2} q 2:3 e 1:0 1:2{2} q 1:3{3} | "D7" q 1:2 1:0 h 2:3 |
lyrics: Don we now our gay ap- par- el, Fa la la, la la la, la la la.
[Line 4]
| "G" q. 2:3 e 2:1 q 2:0 3:2 | "C" 3:0 3:2 "G" 2:0 3:0 | "C" e 1:0 1:0 1:0 1:0 "G" q. 2:3 e 2:1 | "G" q 2:0 "D7" 3:2 "G" h 3:0 ||
lyrics: Troll the an- cient Yule- tide car- ol, Fa la la la la, la la la la.

